## 3. AI-Powered Enterprise Documentation Portal (FBP-DES)

> Scope: **the AI enhancements I contributed inside a much larger MkDocs documentation portal.** The rest of the portal (generators, JSON authoring pipeline, MkDocs theming) is out of scope for this write-up.

**Elevator pitch:** Retrofitted a large enterprise MkDocs docs portal (FBP-DES Components, Channels APIs, BFF SDK, Studio) with a Google-AI-Overview-style GenAI answer experience and a set of Copilot-agent setup scripts that automate onboarding of the platform.

### What I built

#### 3.1 AI Overview — floating GenAI search on top of MkDocs
- Self-contained vanilla-JS module (`docs/assets/javascripts/ai-overview.js`) plus paired CSS (`ai-overview.css`) — no build step, drops straight into MkDocs Material.
- **Hero-search integration** — the docs home page's search bar becomes an AI question box when the AI backend is up. When AI is down, the site gracefully degrades to the native MkDocs search (controlled via a `body.ai-active` class toggled by a health check).
- **AI health-check gate** — a 5 s timed `GET /api/v1/flows/{ANALYST_FLOW_ID}` runs on page load *and* on every MkDocs instant-navigation event; the UI reflects reality without a page reload.
- **Direct call to the AI Canvas Document Analyst flow** (`POST /api/v1/run/{flowId}`) with a 3-minute timeout, LangFlow-shaped response parsing, and section-marker extraction (`===AI_OVERVIEW_START===` / `===AI_OVERVIEW_END===`).
- **Custom lightweight Markdown-to-HTML renderer** (headings, tables, fenced code, ordered/unordered lists, blockquotes, HR, inline emphasis, links) so the AI Overview panel can render Markdown answers **without pulling in a Markdown library** — keeping the docs portal's bundle footprint at zero.
- **Rotating loading messages, suggestion chips, timeout + error surfaces** — production UX details that make the panel feel like a real product, not a bolt-on.

#### 3.2 Copilot-Agent Setup Prompts
A trio of `agent`-mode prompts under `docs/assets/setup-prompts/` that turn Copilot Chat into an **interactive installer** for the FBP-DES platform:

| Prompt | What it does |
|---|---|
| `INITIAL-SETUP-V2.prompt.md.txt` | Guides Copilot through repo cloning, `.env` configuration, Maven builds — with step tracking (`3/6 steps completed`), prerequisite checks, and PowerShell fallbacks for Windows. |
| `DATA-HYDRATION-V2.prompt.md.txt` | Populates the PostgreSQL database for FBP-DES Solution Channels, verifying schemas, and orchestrating the hydration tools. |
| `CONFIG-VERIFICATION-V2.prompt.md.txt` | Configures VS Code's `launch.json`, reloads Maven dependencies, compiles the project, and produces a health-check summary. |

Each prompt follows an interactive-agent contract (waits for user confirmation, tracks progress with ✅ / ⚠️ / ❌, verifies prerequisites, handles errors) — turning what used to be a multi-hour manual runbook into a **20–40 minute guided Copilot session**.

### Impact
Documentation stops being a static wall of Markdown — developers can ask *"how does BFF API authentication work?"* on the home page and get an AI-composed, RAG-grounded answer rendered inline. Onboarding a fresh developer to the FBP-DES stack shrinks from a checklist-and-hope experience to a single Copilot conversation.

