## 4. Doc Portal Reviewer Agent — AI QA for API Documentation

**Elevator pitch:** Point the agent at any documentation portal, pick a domain and a checklist, and it crawls the portal, evaluates every checklist item with an LLM, captures evidence screenshots, and emits a shareable HTML + JSON report. It replaces the manual "review my API docs against 40 checklist items" round-trip.

### What I built
- **Python 3.10+ agent** (`python -m src.main report`) that composes several specialized subsystems:
  - **GuidelinesParser** — reads a YAML/Markdown checklist (e.g. `guidelines/channel-apis-checklist.yaml`).
  - **Crawler** — Playwright (Microsoft Edge / Chromium) headed or headless crawl, scoped by URL path, capped at `crawler.max_pages` (default 200).
  - **Domain Validator** — partitions crawled pages by domain (accounts / payments / cards / counterparty / any custom) with no hard-coded whitelist.
  - **Validation Engine** — per checklist item, calls the configured LLM with the extracted evidence, gets back `{status, confidence, details}`, and thresholds it against `validation.confidence_threshold` (default 0.7) to decide `pass` / `fail` / `needs-review`.
  - **Screenshot Capturer** — evidence images for every `fail` / `needs-review` item, embedded directly into the HTML report.
  - **Report Generator** — self-contained HTML dashboard (summary header, per-item cards, screenshots, LLM reasoning, evidence snippet, source URL) *and* a JSON payload for downstream CI dashboards / diffing.
- **Pluggable LLM provider layer** — swap between `ai-canvas`, `openai`, `azure-openai`, `ollama`, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint via a single `llm.provider` field in `config/settings.yaml`. All API keys are env-var driven (`GENAICANVAS_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY`).
- **Config-first UX** — for a normal run, only three fields need editing (`target.url`, `target.domain`, `target.guidelines`). Everything else has sensible defaults. Every field has a matching CLI override (`--url`, `--domain`, `--guidelines`) for CI use.
- **VS Code task integration** — `Tasks: Run Task → Generate Report (uses config/settings.yaml)` for a one-click run.

### JSON report shape
```json
{
  "checklist_id": "A-OV-01",
  "section": "API Overview",
  "status": "fail",
  "confidence": 0.92,
  "details": "The Counterparty landing page lists 4 APIs, but 'PaymentInitiate' appears under it and belongs to the Payments domain.",
  "evidence": "…snippet of the crawled page…",
  "url": "http://.../fbp-des-channels/api-reference/counterparty/",
  "screenshot": "reports/screenshots/A-OV-01_counterparty.png"
}
```

### Design highlights
- **Deterministic report envelope over non-deterministic LLM verdicts** — the confidence threshold turns "the LLM was unsure" into an explicit, actionable `needs-review` status instead of silently failing.
- **Every run is timestamped** — trivial before/after comparisons after fixing portal issues.
- **HTML report is self-contained** — email it, attach it to a Jira ticket, no server needed.

Pairs naturally with the **AI-Powered Doc Portal (project 3)** — the same portal the AI Overview lives on can be QA'd by this agent — but the reviewer works standalone on any documentation site.

