## 6. Tranversation — Conversational Banking UI (AI Integrations)

> Scope: **the AI-integration portions of the `bff-ui-sdk-reference-app` UI** — the parts that turn a modern React banking app into an AI-driven conversational experience. Non-AI banking UI work (accounts, payees, transfers, registration flows) is out of scope for this summary.

**Elevator pitch:** "Tranversation" = Transactions + Conversations. A conversational banking UI framework that talks to a single AI endpoint and renders responses across 11 different visual template types — with **full user-journey context** shipped alongside every AI query so the model actually knows what the user is looking at.

### What I built

#### 6.1 Interaction Tracker — the "context engine" behind every AI call
A hand-built context capture layer (`src/services/interactionTracker.ts` + `src/services/interactionContextSummarizer.ts`) that:

- **Records the full user journey from login to logout** — navigation, clicks, form changes, field focus, selections, hovers on key elements, scroll, page views — as typed `InteractionEvent`s (`navigation`, `click`, `form_change`, `field_focus`, `selection`, `hover`, `scroll`, `login`, `logout`, `page_view`, `custom`).
- **Two payload modes** exposed to the AI layer:
  - `getPayload()` — raw events (legacy full event list).
  - `getContextPayload()` — a **compact, flow-grouped summary** derived from the raw stream. This is the mode that ships to the AI.
- **Context summarizer pipeline** (`summarizeInteractions`) that:
  1. Groups raw events into per-page `FlowState` objects (keyed by route).
  2. Merges back-and-forth visits to the same route so hesitation is captured but noise is not.
  3. Summarizes each flow (selections, form inputs, available options, click frequency, brief-flow detection).
  4. Detects **cross-flow behavioural patterns** — hesitation, repeated actions across pages.
  5. Adds a **"current activity"** context (route, page name, current field values, available options) so the AI always knows exactly where the user is standing.
  6. Caps the payload at 15 context objects to keep the AI prompt lean.
- **Bounded memory** — the tracker retains the last 200 events; the summarizer output is what actually reaches the AI.

The end result: instead of shipping "500+ raw events" to the AI on every question, the AI receives a **small list of context objects that capture the user's flows and intent** — cheap, precise, and privacy-friendly.

#### 6.2 AI-driven UI surface
On the React side, I added the AI touchpoints that make the app feel conversational:

- **AIOrb** (`src/components/ui/AIOrb`) — the persistent floating AI entry point.
- **ChatOverlay** (`src/components/ui/ChatOverlay`) — the full conversational surface, complete with a **templates/** directory that holds one renderer per Tranversation template type (T1–T11).
- **AISearchBar** (`src/components/dashboard/AISearchBar`) — dashboard-level AI question entry.
- **AIHomeView** (`src/components/dashboard/AIHomeView`) — an AI-first alternate home layout for the dashboard.

#### 6.3 Contract with the AI backend — the Tranversation API
I designed the frontend against a **single-endpoint** AI chat contract (`POST /chat/query`) with a strict template protocol so the same endpoint can render 11 completely different UI shapes:

- **`templateType`** (T1–T11) discriminator determines the `data` schema.
- **`templateVariant`** further specializes types T3–T8 (e.g. table vs. pie chart).
- **`templateMeta`** maps rendering roles to field key-paths inside `data` — decoupling the AI's field naming from the UI renderer.
- **`userInteractionsContext`** — the interaction-tracker payload described above, giving the AI full awareness of the user's journey on every question.

### Template catalog (rendered by the frontend)
| # | Type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| T1 | Text Message | Plain conversational reply |
| T2 | Stats Card | Single-metric hero card |
| T3 | Data Table | Tabular results (variants) |
| T4 | Info Card | Grouped key-value facts |
| T5 | Chart | Line / bar / pie via variant |
| T6 | Timeline | Ordered event history |
| T7 | Alert / Notification | System / risk message |
| T8 | Progress Bar | Goal or step progress |
| T9 | Comparison View | Side-by-side compare |
| T10 | Input Form | Structured follow-up input |
| T11 | Suggestion Cards | Next-best-action prompts |

### Why it matters
Most AI chat integrations ship the user's question naked — the model has no idea what page the user is on, what data they see, or what they just tried. Tranversation ships a **compact, structured context payload with every question**, so answers are grounded in the user's actual state, not guessed from scratch. That is the difference between a chatbot and an assistant.

